<title>BRAZIL: Brazil gets green light for CVRD selloff.</title>
<headline>Brazil gets green light for CVRD selloff.</headline>
<byline>William Schomberg</byline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's government has been given a green light for the privatization of mining conglomerate Companhia Vale do Rio Doce (CVRD) following the sacrifice by a senator of his own bill which sought to block the sale.</p>
<p>Sen. Jose Eduardo Dutra of the left-wing Workers Party surprised the Senate on Wednesday afternoon by withdrawing his proposal that the CVRD selloff be subject to congressional approval.</p>
<p>&quot;I did it because my bill had become the subject of blatant horse-trading of which I want no part,&quot; Dutra said.</p>
</text>
